  "sistemaId": "-KPZgfz6GVeyyTSXrFHT",
  "sistemaWhy": "Xel-Há Norte: the map is the Caleta de Xel-Ha network, and the database's Xel-Há Norte holds its named cenotes (Laguna Negra, Laguna Grande, Northwest Arm, Aquario - all without a position). The import had guessed Cenote Xel-Há South (-KPZgfueJT9K3VKShMqu) and put this map's exploration record (Expéditions Yuc 97/2000) there, but that cenote (at OSM's Cenote El Jaguar, beside Zacate) lies about 1.3 km west of the caleta, off this map's page. The south arm (Collecteur sud, towards Dos Ojos) has no sistema of its own in the database.",
  "utmEpsg": 32616,
  "placementWhy": "Free similarity fit on water bodies visible on the satellite imagery (OSM polygons traced from it): the four cenote pools south of the caleta, Laguna Grande (OSM 'Dolphin Inlet') and Laguna Negra (OSM 'Black Lagoon'). The scale bar is not used: the fit gives 0.75 m/px where the bar's 450 m gives 0.556 m/px - the bar reads as 0-200-400-600 m (810 px = 607 m), and the caleta's outline confirms the larger scale. The north arrow (magnetic, 1997) is about 9 degrees off true north. The coast drawn north of the caleta is schematic (up to 100 m east of the real beach) and X-Cacelito is drawn about 470 m south of Cenote Xcacel: neither is used.",
  "trace": {
    "method": "colour-fill",
    "why": "Passages filled in violet-blue, cenote and lagoon surface water in pale blue, both outlined in black; collapse zones in orange are traced with the passages (fillColours), their boulders as details; the sea is masked by its colour.",
