  "symbols": {
    "why": "French UIS map, depths in metres written as negative numbers (-7, two of them, in the Salle corrodée rooms; no overlined numbers), no letter codes and no legend. Bones are named, not drawn: 'Squelettes de manati' (two leader lines) and 'Squelette de crocodile' (a dash to the passage), placed at the leader ends. Flow arrows: the 'Arrivées d'eau' (water inflows) at the western passage ends, 'Débit 1000 l/s' and 'Débit 1400 l/s' in the lagoon, and the arrows in the collapse zones; 'Débit 400 l/s' (north arm) and X-Cacelito's 500 l/s have no arrow. 'Trémie' (breakdown choke) and 'Zone effondrée' (collapse zone, open to the surface) are kept as place names. 'DOS OJOS' at the south-west passage end, which runs off the page: leads-to.",
